Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:00:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Apply the sink's in-memory bulk cache changes only after
 a fenced batch commits

A fenced batch can abort after its writes ran (revocation, a failed
write, a transient retry). Cache updates and evictions made by the
immediate write paths are now queued through ISinkWrites.AfterCommit and
dropped with an aborted attempt, so a bulk window never answers reads
with state that never reached the collection. Unfenced writes apply the
change at once, as before.
